  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/pterophyllum_altum_en/",
      "html": "<p>Deep Angels can reach 20 cm in length and up to 35 cm in height.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/pterophyllum_altum_en/",
      "html": "<p>Colombia, Venezuela, Orinoco.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/pterophyllum_altum_en/",
      "html": "<p>This has to be considered when buying the tank: it should have a height of at least 70 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/pterophyllum_altum_en/",
      "html": "<p>For keeping them, medium-hard water with a neutral pH is sufficient. For breeding attempts the water should contain almost no minerals and have pH values around 5.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/pterophyllum_altum_en/",
      "html": "<p>Decoration with large bogwood provides structure and retreat possibilities.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/pterophyllum_altum_en/",
      "html": "<p>They are sensitive to bad water quality and stress, so they are not really suitable for community tanks. In no case should they be kept with overly lively fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/pterophyllum_altum_en/",
      "html": "<p>Only a few hobbyists have been able to breed them. Remarkably, even the parents of an F2 generation clearly show a spawning season of a few months (in spring).</p>"
    }
  ],
